* pre-R13: finish POLYLINE, VERTEX
* add API for more complex entities, like 3dsolids, hatch, ACSH solids, dynblocks.
* PROXY graphics: decode MESH, SHELL, LWPOLYLINE, apply the sub entity
  colors, layers and the model transformations in dwg2SVG
* rename all internal ent->tio.ENTITY to ent->tio._ENTITY, so that all 3D names can
  stay asis. Which fixes the public API for all _3D names, to be more consistent.
* extract seldomly used objects into extra sharedlib(s) as dynaloaded or linked plugin.
  dynblocks, ACSH solids, ... to keep compile times managable.
* TABLE_Cell
* Enabled, but unstable and un(der)tested (see doc/LibreDWG.texi and
  src/classes.inc for the full list):
  ARCALIGNEDTEXT (only 2018/arcalignedtext.dxf, DXF out is skipped)
  ASSOCACTION ASSOC2DCONSTRAINTGROUP ASSOCDEPENDENCY ASSOC*SURFACEACTIONBODY
  DATALINK DBCOLOR EVALUATION_GRAPH FCFOBJECTCONTEXTDATA HELIX
  LAYOUTPRINTCONFIG LIGHTLIST OBJECT_PTR PLANESURFACE PROXY_OBJECT
  TABLECONTENT
* Debugging only, with configure --enable-debug (fields spec'ed but
  broken/untested):
  GEOPOSITIONMARKER EXTRUDEDSURFACE LOFTEDSURFACE NURBSURFACE
  REVOLVEDSURFACE SWEPTSURFACE SUNSTUDY ASSOCALIGNEDDIMACTIONBODY
  ASSOCPERSSUBENTMANAGER PERSUBENTMGR ACSH_SWEEP_CLASS NAVISWORKSMODELDEF
  DATATABLE *OBJECTCONTEXTDATA (all but ALDIM, BLKREF, LEADER, MTEXT, TEXT) ...
* Promoted to stable since 0.14: MATERIAL (procedural textures are dropped
  without DEBUG_CLASSES), TABLE, MLEADERSTYLE, DIMASSOC, ARC_DIMENSION,
  ACIDBLOCKREFERENCE, LAYER_FILTER, and ALDIM, BLKREF, LEADER, MTEXT and
  TEXT OBJECTCONTEXTDATA.
* Unhandled (i.e. passed through, no DXF and fields):
  ACDSRECORD ACDSSCHEMA NPOCOLLECTION RAPIDRTRENDERENVIRONMENT
  XREFPANELOBJECT
* add test coverage - i.e. an extended example_2018.dwg with all types,
  for the following entities, which are in no test DWG (CAMERA DGNUNDERLAY
  DWFUNDERLAY LONG_TRANSACTION have a 2018/*.dxf or *.dxf now, but ODA writes
  proxies): CAMERA DGNUNDERLAY DWFUNDERLAY GEOPOSITIONMARKER
  LONG_TRANSACTION PROXY_ENTITY PROXY_LWPOLYLINE DUMMY BACKGROUND
* likewise for the following missing objects (DWFDEFINITION LIGHTLIST
  VBA_PROJECT have a 2018/*.dxf now):
  CSACDOCUMENTOPTIONS
  DGNDEFINITION
  XREFPANELOBJECT IDBUFFER IMAGEDEF
  IMAGEDEF_REACTOR
  NPOCOLLECTION OBJECT_PTR PROXY_OBJECT
  RASTERVARIABLES UCS SUN
* check-dxf/outdxf: DXFIN coverage for all generated dxfs. some objects even crash acad:
  VERTEX_3D, MLINE.
* DXFIN errors:
  Fixed: Drawing_2007, 2010, 2018 (no errors). Drawing_2000_min is gone.
  example_2000: Invalid LIGHT.class_version, PERSUBENTMGR: Unexpected DXF
  code 0, expected 90 for num_subents, ASSOCPERSSUBENTMANAGER fields
  numassocsteps and numassocsubents are invalid

* convert XRECORD xdata linked-list ResBuf to array of eed[],
  same structure as common EED.
* merge decode_r2007 with the 2004 decoder. It is almost the same, just
  the sections have multiple pages. Only for this version. 2010+ uses
  the 2004 format.
* All DWG versions can be read and written now (r2007: src/encode_r2007.c).
  Todo: large DWGs written as r2007 or r2010 still need recovery in ODA,
  and downconverting r2010+ objects to r2007 loses data (TABLESTYLE custom
  cell styles).
* GeoJSON: all graphical entities are supported now. Todo: explode INSERT
  into a GeometryCollection, RAY and XLINE are only a unit segment.
* more dwgfilter examples, as from the osmctools, with keep and drop rules.
* check osm tools https://gitlab.com/osm-c-tools/osmctools how
  they could import GIS data easier.
  Check OpenStreetMap XML and PBF formats.
* add one of the easy OGR formats: gml, gpx. See the xmlsuite which does it also.
  See https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Dxf2gpx
  https://grass.osgeo.org/grass74/manuals/v.in.dxf.html and dwg (teigha and opencad)
  But only as external sharedlib plugin.
* add more geom.c utils to tessellate curves (e.g. GeoJSON)
* ACIS: We already convert the binary SAB to ASCII SAT version 2 (ASM ShapeManager,
  forked from ACIS 7.0), but the add API is still struggling to create them.
  At least I found proper docs for the ACIS SDK.
* map DWG constraints to FreeCAD and SolveSpace constraints
  https://www.freecadweb.org/wiki/Sketcher_Workbench#Sketcher_Constraints
* check valabind vapi files to generate more and better bindings
